examples.solution_text:
Translate $y=\sqrt{x}$ left $1$ unit and down $2$ units.
Choose values making $x+1$ a perfect square.

| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ | $8$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $y$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |

The endpoint is $(-1,-2)$.
For the $y$-intercept, set $x=0$: $y=\sqrt{1}-2=-1$, giving $(0,-1)$.
For the $x$-intercept, set $y=0$.
$\begin{aligned}0&=\sqrt{x+1}-2\\\sqrt{x+1}&=2\\x+1&=4\\x&=3\end{aligned}$
The $x$-intercept is $(3,0)$.
Draw a smooth curve through the table points, increasing to the right with a decreasing gradient.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-2,0)--(10,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick,->] plot[domain=0:3.2,samples=101,variable=\t] ({\t*\t-1},{\t-2});
\fill[black] (-1,-2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-1,-2) node[below left] {$(-1,-2)$};
\fill[black] (0,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,-1) node[right] {$(0,-1)$};
\fill[black] (3,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (3,0) node[below right] {$(3,0)$};
\fill[black] (8,1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (8,1) node[above left] {$(8,1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
The graph is a translation and reflection of $y=\sqrt{x}$, with no dilation. Write its equation and state its domain and range in interval notation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-6,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick,->] plot[domain=0:2.8,samples=101,variable=\t] ({2-\t*\t},{1+\t});
\fill[black] (2,1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,1) node[right] {$(2,1)$};
\fill[black] (1,2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (1,2) node[right] {$(1,2)$};
\fill[black] (-2,3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,3) node[above left] {$(-2,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The solid graph $g(x)$ is a vertical dilation of the dashed graph $f(x)=\sqrt{x}$. Describe the dilation and write the equation of $g(x)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-0.5,0)--(10.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.5)--(0,7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed,->] plot[domain=0:3.1,samples=101,variable=\t] ({\t*\t},{\t});
\path (6,2.45) node[below right] {$f(x)=\sqrt{x}$};
\draw[black,thick,->] plot[domain=0:3.1,samples=101,variable=\t] ({\t*\t},{2*\t});
\path (5,4.47) node[left] {$g(x)$};
\fill[black] (1,2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (1,2) node[right] {$(1,2)$};
\fill[black] (9,6) circle (1.5pt);
\path (9,6) node[above left] {$(9,6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
